{
  // Cloudflare Workers config. The site is static (Astro output in dist/); the
  // worker script runs first for the paths in run_worker_first: every page, so the host can be
  // checked (worker/host.js: a host that is not the site's address is redirected, and after the
  // move the old domain answers 301s and the hand-off), media (HTTP range requests, which Safari
  // needs to play video, and files kept in R2), the API, and group pages. On the primary host a
  // page is handed to the static assets untouched. The "!" lines are files only (fingerprinted
  // bundles, search index, figures, quiz and card data, the hop graph): they skip the worker on any host.
  // COST: every page view now runs the worker once. On the Workers Free plan (100,000 requests a
  // day) traffic above that limit gets Cloudflare error 1027 instead of the page; use Workers Paid.
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "biochempedia",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-07-03",
  "main": "worker/index.js",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./dist",
    "binding": "ASSETS",
    "not_found_handling": "404-page",
    "run_worker_first": ["/*", "!/_astro/*", "!/pagefind/*", "!/vendor/*", "!/figures/*", "!/scientists/*", "!/quiz/*", "!/flashcards/*", "!/helper-data/*", "!/graph.json", "!/graph/*"]
  },
  // Film files also live in this R2 bucket under the same paths they have on the site
  // (uploaded with `node scripts/upload-media.mjs`). The worker serves them from here and
  // falls back to the static assets, so a file may be in either place.
  "r2_buckets": [{ "binding": "MEDIA", "bucket_name": "biochempedia-media" }],
  // Teacher classes (worker/api.js): teachers, classes, nickname-only students and their
  // lesson answers. Schema in migrations/; apply with
  // `npx wrangler d1 migrations apply biochempedia-classes --remote`.
  "d1_databases": [{ "binding": "CLASSES", "database_name": "biochempedia-classes", "database_id": "9f3ecb19-8241-4bb3-9c23-eccd8467ce98", "migrations_dir": "migrations" }],
  // Optional: set RESEND_API_KEY as a secret (`npx wrangler secret put RESEND_API_KEY`) to turn on
  // email verification and password-reset links. Without it, teachers use a recovery code.
  //
  // The owner's totals page (/admin/, worker/admin.js, GET /api/admin/stats) is gated by a SECRET
  // named ADMIN_TOKEN. It is never a var in this file and never in the repository. Set it with
  // `npx wrangler secret put ADMIN_TOKEN` and paste a long random value (for example the output of
  // `openssl rand -hex 32`); it must be 24 to 512 printable characters with NO SPACES, or it is treated
  // as not set. It also keys the film counter's rate-limit hashes (worker/film-count.js), unless a
  // separate RATE_SALT secret is set. Until it is set the
  // route answers the same 404 as any unknown path. To switch the page off, delete the secret
  // (`npx wrangler secret delete ADMIN_TOKEN`). The role question and the film count need the
  // column and tables in migrations/0009_role_and_film_counts.sql (same migrations command as above);
  // until then the account page asks nothing and the film counter stores nothing.
  // NOTE: that command applies EVERY migration not yet applied. If 0007 has not been applied, it is
  // applied too, and with PLANNER_ENABLED "1" below the AI study planner goes live on the site's
  // Anthropic key, within its caps. Do not apply 0009 by itself with `d1 execute --file`: a later
  // `migrations apply` would run it again and fail on the column that already exists.
  "vars": {
    // The site's address is not a var here: the build needs it too (canonical tags, sitemap, QR codes),
    // and a Worker var cannot reach the build. It is PRIMARY_HOST in src/lib/site-host.mjs, read by both.
    // MAIL_FROM stays on biochemistrypedia.com until Resend has verified stemhop.com.
    "MAIL_FROM": "STEMhop <classes@biochemistrypedia.com>",
    // Curiosity router (worker/curious.js, POST /api/curious). Currently ON: it needs both
    // ROUTER_ENABLED "1" and the ANTHROPIC_API_KEY secret (`npx wrangler secret put ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`).
    // To turn it off in one step, set ROUTER_ENABLED to "0" and deploy (or delete the secret).
    // Setup and cost notes are in Chris's private working notes, not this repository.
    // ROUTER_MOCK is for local tests only (canned answers, no API call); never set it here.
    "ROUTER_ENABLED": "1",
    "ROUTER_DAILY_CAP_USD": "0.50",
    "ROUTER_MONTHLY_CAP_USD": "5",
    "ROUTER_IP_PER_MIN": "10",
    "ROUTER_IP_PER_DAY": "50",
    "ROUTER_GLOBAL_PER_MIN": "30",
    // "1" stores the text of questions (router_queries, 30 days). Off by default; keep it off for a
    // site children use. The box's "your question is not stored" line follows this switch, but
    // /privacy/ does not: it says questions are not stored, so change that page first if this ever changes.
    "ROUTER_LOG_QUERIES": "0",
    // Study helpers for learner accounts (worker/helper.js, /api/help/*): "explain this another way",
    // feedback on a claim-evidence-reasoning answer, and flashcards from highlights. Same
    // ANTHROPIC_API_KEY secret as the router, with separate caps. Needs HELPER_ENABLED "1" AND the
    // helper_budget table (migrations/0008_study_helpers.sql); until both, GET /api/help is a 503 and
    // no control shows. To turn them off in one step, set HELPER_ENABLED to "0" and deploy.
    // HELPER_MOCK is for local tests only (canned answers, no API call); never set it here.
    "HELPER_ENABLED": "0",
    // Which helpers are offered once enabled, so each can be turned on by itself (comma-separated):
    // "explain", "feedback", "cards". Only the ones listed show on lesson pages.
    "HELPER_FEATURES": "explain,feedback,cards",
    "HELPER_DAILY_CAP_USD": "1.50",
    "HELPER_MONTHLY_CAP_USD": "15",
    "HELPER_EXPLAIN_PER_DAY": "20",
    "HELPER_FEEDBACK_PER_DAY": "10",
    "HELPER_CARDS_PER_DAY": "5",
    "HELPER_AGAIN_PER_LESSON": "3",
    "HELPER_IP_PER_MIN": "10",
    "HELPER_IP_PER_DAY": "80",
    "HELPER_GLOBAL_PER_MIN": "30",
    "HELPER_EFFORT": "low",
    // The model for the grounding check that reads every reply before it is shown (the replies
    // themselves stay on Sonnet). In testing a stronger checker raised far fewer false alarms.
    "HELPER_CHECK_MODEL": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
    // Study planner (worker/planner.js, /api/plan/*): learners' study plans and teachers' syllabus
    // matching, on the same ANTHROPIC_API_KEY secret as the router. It also needs the tables in
    // migrations/0007_planner.sql (`npx wrangler d1 migrations apply biochempedia-classes --remote`);
    // until they exist it reports itself off and the pages hide it. Evaluated on the real key on
    // 2026-11-14 before shipping on. "0" switches it off; saved plans and class lists still open. PLANNER_MOCK is for local tests only; never set it here.
    "PLANNER_ENABLED": "1",
    "PLANNER_DAILY_CAP_USD": "2",
    "PLANNER_MONTHLY_CAP_USD": "20",
    "PLANNER_ACCOUNT_PER_DAY": "5",
    "PLANNER_EFFORT": "low"
  },
  "observability": { "enabled": true }
}
